{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: from hugh, 2026-10-02. Draft a design note, notes/2026-10-02-collections-of-rooms.md, on how collections of Rooms are shaped and governed for services at software scale: the grid whose columns are services, rows are customers and cells are engagement Rooms; the control Rooms that contribute to a collection (a firm for identity, a catalogue for functionality, groupings for reporting dimensions); and revocation, which may need its own mechanism because of its scale and timeliness requirements. Make it concrete by following the workflow step by step through a variety of use cases, both dap cases (a bounded property claim, a care episode, a renovation, the sale) and existing Artroom cases (a code room with a shared checker service and a pi-durable author; Artroom's own self-hosted development; the jam room), and use the walk-throughs to generate numbered requirements that later requests can cite. Hold the design to the rules agreed in discussion: a Room's admission never reads another Room; control Rooms hold grants and definitions, never commands; collection membership lives in the registry keyed by genesis fields; taking a new definition is a proposal in the cell; reporting carries copies, never authority. Related: requests d50ce26d (firm authority chain design) and a13a0bf5 (bootstrap with a policy), assert d8e11208. A draft for hugh's reading first; checker review after.","body":{"conditions":"notes/2026-10-02-collections-of-rooms.md on main: (1) the three kinds of control Room with the one mechanism each uses, in a table; (2) at least six walk-throughs, each a numbered sequence of steps naming the Room acted in, the control Room contributing, the mechanism, what the cell records, and the protocol rule met or the gap found; (3) a section on revocation that states the scale and timeliness requirements from the walk-throughs and compares at least three mechanisms against them; (4) numbered requirements, each traceable to a walk-through step, each stated so a test could show it holds; (5) what the note does not decide; labels [Source], [Judgement] and [Untested] on claims, with protocol rules cited by number.","target_head":"bd520fb926f8161a722c6f1e23ae4aac29e41a66","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}